=2 Walkthrough
* This time, {n:Hishahma} requests your assistance in figuring out the best way to kill certain kinds of monsters.
* Similar to {q:Finding Faults|Finding Faults|Finding Faults}, you travel to a beastman stronghold and spawn a NM.
** This time the NM needs to be killed.
* **Orobon**: {z:Arrapago Reef}, (E-11 Map 2) - {m:Ornery Orobon}
** You may need one {i:Lamian Fang Key|Lamian Fang Key|2219} to reach the **???**
** A {i:Lamian Fang Key|Lamian Fang Key|2219} is not required if you travel via the {p:Ilrusi Atoll Staging Point}.
* **Wamouracampa**: {z:Halvung}, (L-8) - {m:Wheel Wamoura}
** Reach this using the Halvung Survival Guide warp
** This NM takes 0 damage until you cause it to lower its defenses.
** Options to cause it to unfold (and take non-0 damage) are:
*** Shining a Light on it (clicking a nearby "Light Point" NPC that spawns)
*** Casting enfeebling magic
*** Hitting it
* **Puk**: {z:Mamook}, (G-8) (upstairs) - {m:Carpophagous Puk}
** Reach this using the {z:Mamook} entrance from {p:Mamool Ja Staging Point} or {p:Aht Urghan Whitegate} -> {z:Bhaflau Thickets} HP #1.
** The NM will try to run away around 90% HP and will despawn if it reaches the end of its path.
*** While running, it takes approximately -90% damage.
*** If it despawns, you will need to zone to spawn it again.
** Options to cause it to stop running are:
*** Disguising as Mamool Ja
*** Clicking the NPC fruit that spawn (must be Red)
*** Using multiple weaponskills
* Return to {n:Hishahma} and tell him what worked (or guess)
* Zone and return to him to find out if you were right and receive your reward (or berating)

__If solo, the Wamouracampa is recommended__
=2 Notes
{q:Finding Faults|Finding Faults|Finding Faults} must be completed with all three monster types before {n:Hishahma} presents you with the option for this quest.
